# Shortcut story titles

When drafting or creating Shortcut stories (feature, bug, chore):

## Format

```text
[<Type>] [<FeatureArea>] <short clear title>
```

| Part | Meaning | Examples |
|------|---------|----------|
| Type | Work kind | `FE`, `BE`, `QA` |
| FeatureArea | Product / module area (from squad prefs / project-context) | `Orders`, `Catalog`, `Checkout` |
| Title | Short outcome-focused phrase | Add filter to status dropdown |

## Examples

| Good | Bad |
|------|-----|
| `[FE] [Orders] Add search to status filter on list page` | `[FE] Add search to status filter on list page` |
| `[BE] [Checkout] Emit event on successful payment capture` | `fix payment` |
| `[QA] [Catalog] Cover negative path for empty brand list` | `test brands` |

## Rules

1. Always include **both** type and feature area tags when the area is known.
2. Feature area matches the product module from project-context / prefs, not the epic name alone.
3. Keep the rest of the title short and concrete.
4. Do not invent a feature area. Ask if unclear.
5. Org-specific area names and examples live in private memory (`.cursor/qa-memory/org-context.md`), not in this public rule.
